# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows, where git's autocrlf converts on checkout. A CRLF `#!` line
# makes the Linux CI container fail with a bare `bad interpreter` — a failure that appears only on a
# fresh clone, never on the machine that wrote the file, and that looks like a Docker problem rather
# than a line-ending one. Pinning it here means the local CI gate cannot be broken by a clone.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read inside the container, and one of them is the container's own recipe.
Dockerfile.ci   text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
